    {
      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To solve this problem, let's first define what the complement of an angle is. The complement of an angle is the angle that, when added to the given angle, results in a right angle (90 degrees).\n\nLet's denote the measure of the angle as \\( x \\) degrees. According to the problem, the measure of this angle is double its complement. The complement of \\( x \\) degrees is \\( 90 - x \\) degrees. Therefore, the angle \\( x \\) is double this complement:\n\n\\[ x = 2 \\times (90 - x) \\]\n\nNow, we will solve this equation step by step.\n\n1. Distribute the 2 on the right-hand side of the equation:\n\\[ x = 2 \\times 90 - 2 \\times x \\]\n\\[ x = 180 - 2x \\]\n\n2. To isolate \\( x \\), add \\( 2x \\) to both sides of the equation:\n\\[ x + 2x = 180 \\]\n\\[ 3x = 180 \\]\n\n3. Finally, divide both sides by 3 to solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{180}{3} \\]\n\\[ x = 60 \\]\n\nThus, the measure of the angle is 60 degrees.",
